    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 11 with a focused offensive strategy, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (67.23) and **Yordan Alvarez** (64.21). **Junior Caminero** earns the highest daily efficiency score by capitalizing on a favorable #2 spot in the order, effectively neutralizing the challenge posed by Gausman despite a moderate xERA. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite facing the difficult George Kirby; his elite xwOBA of 0.429 provides a high enough floor to warrant confidence even against top-tier pitching. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) rounds out our strongest group, as he benefits significantly from a projected move to the #3 hole and a highly favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki, whose 5.30 xERA represents the softest target on today's slate.\n\nWe are navigating a roster hampered by significant absences, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** sidelined due to team off-days, while **Christian Yelich** remains on the IL. In the absence of our speed threats, **Hyeseong Kim** (41.19) barely clears the floor for selection. His score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Trevor McDonald (2.60 xERA) and the threat of an elite defensive catcher, but he is forced into the lineup to maintain our category coverage. **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.61) and **Luke Raley** (52.38) occupy marginal status today; **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a stiff test against Drew Rasmussen, and **Luke Raley** sits just above our cutoff, relying on platoon advantages to provide value. We continue to monitor the status of **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** as potential depth, though none currently surpass our starting six's efficiency metrics for today's specific matchups.",
